WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:10.635
Oh my ears and whiskers, 
my pocket watch has stopped.

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:13.555
Excuse me, sir, 
do you have the time?

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:15.098
Please tell me that's 
your pet rabbit.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:17.517
That's Mr. W Rabbit
 to you, ma'am.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.102
There's a talking 
rabbit that nobody

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:20.102
can see but us. 

00:00:20.102 --> 00:00:21.102
You're adorable.

00:00:21.102 --> 00:00:23.815
Don't talk to me 
like I-I-I-I-I like that. 

00:00:23.815 --> 00:00:25.525
I like that very much.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:33.241
 I ask why you're here.

00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:33.783
It's a mystery.

00:00:34.909 --> 00:00:36.202
I love mysteries!

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:37.245
My name is Alice.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:39.998
This isn't Wonderland. 
It's middle school.

00:00:41.791 --> 00:00:44.085
Let's see. We started 
seeing strange messages.

00:00:45.462 --> 00:00:47.047
So we're dealing with a...?

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:47.797
Ghostwriter.

00:00:48.465 --> 00:00:50.175
It's rolling out the 
white carpet.

00:00:52.761 --> 00:00:53.803
What is happening?

00:00:54.512 --> 00:00:55.221
Donna told me. 

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.806
You're solving 
the mystery for a ghost

00:00:56.806 --> 00:00:58.516
who's releasing 
characters from books.

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.021
And you believed her?

00:01:05.065 --> 00:01:07.817
She's a clone of Chevon.
They're identical.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:09.778
Together we can do anything.

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:11.738
Look, I could give you a
whole speech about

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.530
 how Asher's wrong. 

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:14.657
Or, you could save us 
the time and just trust me

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:16.284
because I get higher 
grades than he does.

00:01:16.284 --> 00:01:17.327
She did not just say that.

00:01:20.538 --> 00:01:22.040
We went in to the book.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.958
We became book characters?

00:01:24.793 --> 00:01:25.752
Stylin'.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.799
Excuse me, monster lady, 
we come in peace. 

00:01:30.799 --> 00:01:31.716
We're your friends.

00:01:31.716 --> 00:01:33.927
See, I got this.

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:36.387
I don't got this!

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:40.350
What is that?

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.019
I don't think these cowboys
are from the Old West.

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:51.694
What are you kids staring at?

00:01:51.694 --> 00:01:52.694
Nothing.

00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:54.239
Okay.

00:01:54.239 --> 00:01:55.240
Night, night. 

00:01:57.492 --> 00:01:58.201
Is that the...?

00:01:58.201 --> 00:01:59.369
The Mona Lisa.

00:02:00.537 --> 00:02:01.830
Did that rat just 
drive that car?

00:02:02.413 --> 00:02:03.748
Prepare for a quantum time leap.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.418
Dinosaurs!

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.755
I actually thought moving
here would be boring.

00:02:12.924 --> 00:02:14.551
Who knew I'd be having
conversations

00:02:14.551 --> 00:02:15.551
with a talking rabbit.

00:02:17.262 --> 00:02:19.514
Time traveling with 
a pirate and his pet rat.

00:02:21.182 --> 00:02:22.642
And it all started in
this book store.

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:25.061
A clue from Ghostwriter.

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:35.321
I did not see the end coming.
I couldn't believe that—

00:02:36.072 --> 00:02:36.823
Spoiler alert.

00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:40.493
You sure have a 
colorful imagination.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.246
What are you doing?

00:02:44.247 --> 00:02:45.874
We're practicing our miming.

00:02:45.874 --> 00:02:48.042
You never know when 
Cirque du Soleil will be hiring.

